From 4a7c874739241030595904f933db55d7a33f9ab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:53:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hayro-syntax: Limit nesting depth of arrays and dictionaries

Skipping over nested arrays and dictionaries was implemented recursively
without any depth limit, so a small file with deeply nested objects could
overflow the stack and abort the whole process (which, unlike a panic,
cannot be caught via catch_unwind).

Track the nesting depth while skipping and bail out once it exceeds
MAX_NESTING_DEPTH (256). In addition, only skip (instead of read) garbage
objects in dictionary key position, since reading nested dictionaries
recursed through the same code path without a limit.

Closes #1347
